 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS A.\nO sweet old Tower of Judah! O,\nA tomb that bared the pillars above,\nAnd in those kings' eyes, thine is a shadow,\nSo true they say; for thou with many\nHadst nigh contempt on earthly pomp displayed;\nBut when thy glory overflowed again,\nThy monument at once became a\nSpiritual symbol to our\nRevolving tongues.  No sire ever\nWas made more noble by his labours far,\nHis heart and eye were one:  but now again,",
